\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+5)({e}^{x})-\\int ({e}^{x})(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}-6\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x({e}^{x})-\\int ({e}^{x})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}-\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}-{e}^{x}+D \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}-6({e}^{x}(x-1)+D) \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{x}-6{e}^{x}(x-1)+C \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(3{x}^{2}-6x+11)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-6D.$" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186069905 1061 618537 13194139534585 17592186045417 false] [17592186069905 1061 655420 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186069906 1061 618538 13194139534585 17592186045417 false] [17592186069906 1061 655421 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186069907 1061 618541 13194139534585 17592186045417 false] [17592186069907 1061 655424 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186069908 1061 618544 13194139534585 17592186045417 false] [17592186069908 1061 655427 13194