 17592186426559 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426561 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426562 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426570 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426565 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426570 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426570 1077 "selection" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426570 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426559 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426570 1079 #uuid "28c7437d-28ce-57c0-b7a0-1e393d54f2ce" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426567 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426571 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426571 1077 "field-1" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426571 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426567 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426571 1079 #uuid "4883c65b-47ec-5430-84ca-1fcf8db21931" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426572 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426564 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426572 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426572 1077 "field-1" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426572 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426564 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426572 1079 #uuid "e23dfcde-ad81-55af-adf6-6a05704da2aa" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426573 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426572 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426573 1069 "q-351987" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426573 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426573 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426573 1072 #uuid "a6ff8230-4cd4-5bdf-91e7-cb6fa8cd2201" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426573 1074 "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={y}^{2}-2\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=2y, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}={e}^{2y-1}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y=\\int {e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y=\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =({y}^{2}-2)(\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2})(2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\int y\\,{e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int y\\,{e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=y\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}={e}^{2y-1}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y=\\int {e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y=\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,{e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(y)(\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{2})(1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{y\\,{e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{y\\,{e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\int y\\,{e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}}{2}-(\\frac{y\\,{e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{4}+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}}{2}-\\frac{y\\,{e}^{2y-1}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{4}-D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{4}(2{y}^{2}-2y-3)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-2){e}^{2y-1}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{e}^{2y-1}}{4}(2{y}^{2}-2y-3)]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2(2)-1}}{4}(2(2)^{2}-2(2)-3))-(\\frac{{e}^{2(0)-1}}{4}(2(0)^{2}-2(0)-3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4}(8-4-3)-\\frac{1}{4e}(0-0-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4}+\\frac{3}{4e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4}+3}{4e}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426574 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426570 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426574 1069 "q-12702" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426574 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426574 1071 "Calculate the integral of $\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426574 1072 #uuid "b249bd56-a311-5aac-8127-3bb428050e53" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426574 1074 "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$  We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4D \\\\  & =2((2-{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=4D.$" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426575 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426571 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426575 1069 "q-352006" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426575 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426575 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426575 1072 #uuid "e4cb84bb-48aa-5c52-99a6-e37928c66119" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true] [17592186426575 1074 "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2{x}^{2}+1\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+1)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4(-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-4D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =((2{\\pi }^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +4\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )-(1\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+4(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =(0-4\\pi -0)-0 \\\\  & =-4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534585 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0f79f135-866e-5aa9-9844-f84faf5dcd03" 17592186426557 "answer-23fb8eab-5460-547b-b2ad-ef24d834a4ac" 17592186426558 "answer-42fc688d-ccf9-5e3f-99f9-e9941c5fff39" 17592186426559 "answer-79698332-96bc-55d0-ad26-153f8dd43ca4" 17592186426560 "answer-8741f008-c5e4-549d-9171-5af8b0240b75" 17592186426561 "answer-89f8a0f0-e701-5fa9-9b52-718247b1cbf7" 17592186426562 "answer-a69adeb4-390c-592d-a129-ec362241488e" 17592186426563 "answer-ae03c0d2-b48d-57a5-8cfb-d6756b8b3bf3" 17592186426564 "answer-ba2348b9-22cb-5fc7-b011-115a2df65e1a" 17592186426565 "answer-c66c13c0-b41c-577a-a9f9-ad68b34d2f4b" 17592186426566 "answer-d2daceba-6894-54c3-9d96-cb343849beed" 17592186426567 "answer-d902eb78-646b-5e1b-bb1c-2b84ee6306c7" 17592186426568 "answer-eb274079-823f-539d-92fb-4448aeb95da5" 17592186426569 "answer-field-28c7437d-28ce-57c0-b7a0-1e393d54f2ce" 17592186426570 "answer-field-4883c65b-47ec-5430-84ca-1fcf8db21931" 17592186426571 "answer-field-e23dfcde-ad81-55af-adf6-6a05704da2aa" 17592186426572 "question-a6ff8230-4cd4-5bdf-91e7-cb6fa8cd2201" 17592186426573 "question-b249bd56-a311-5aac-8127-3bb428050e53" 17592186426574 "question-e4cb84bb-48aa-5c52-99a6-e37928c66119" 17592186426575}}
